<title>THAILAND: Union Asia scraps planned share issue.</title>
<headline>Union Asia scraps planned share issue.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Asia Finance Plc said on Wednesday it was scrapping a planned share issue due to the troubled Thai economy and bearish stock market.</p>
<p>Earlier this month the firm said it would issue 40.6 million new shares through a rights issue. It planned to offer one new share for every two shares already held at a cost of 10 baht per new share.</p>
</text>
